# The Weekly Challenge 288 - Lubos Kolouch

Solutions for Task 1 (Closest Palindrome) and Task 2 (Contiguous Block) in Perl and Python.

## Task 1: Closest Palindrome
- Find the closest palindrome integer to a given integer string, excluding the integer itself.
- If multiple palindromes have the same minimal absolute difference, return the smaller one.
- Implemented by generating candidate palindromes from the prefix $(-1, 0, +1)$ and handling transition edge cases ($99\dots9$, $100\dots01$).

## Task 2: Contiguous Block
- Find the size of the largest contiguous block of identical symbols in a rectangular matrix of `'x'` and `'o'`.
- Implemented using Depth-First Search (DFS) grid traversal with a visited matrix.
